+### Session 071 — 2026-08-11
+**Agent:** E2 Agent (Emergent, Neo)
+**Scope:** `XS` (documentation + read-only database verification; zero application or schema file changes)
+**Triggered by:** Operator supplied a managed Supabase PostgreSQL `DATABASE_URL` and authorized a Gate B run — managed database only, direct connection preferred, read-only, no schema push, no migrations, no fabricated PASS.
+
+**What was done:**
+- **Run 1 (direct host): BLOCKED by environment.** The direct host publishes only an AAAA (IPv6) record (verified via DNS-over-HTTPS; no A record) and this container has zero IPv6 interfaces — raw TCP to the published IPv6 address fails with `Cannot assign requested address`. Recorded honestly; no local PostgreSQL substituted; no fabricated result.
+- **Run 2 (operator-authorized session pooler, port 5432, same managed database): environment VERIFIED.** The operator-supplied pooler host `aws-1-us-west-2` was reachable but its pooler rejected the tenant (`ENOTFOUND tenant/user`); one clearly-labeled read-only diagnostic found the tenant on sibling `aws-0-us-west-2`, where the full verification ran. Results (fresh clearly-labeled read-only verifier; the lost pinned script `df1465bb…` remains unrestored and was NOT reconstructed under its identity):
+  - `DATABASE_URL` present (secret kept in a mode-600 env file outside the git tree; never printed, logged, committed, or patched)
+  - Connection PASS (TLS, authenticated, session forced `transaction_read_only=on`)
+  - Identity/version recorded safely: database `postgres`, **PostgreSQL 17.6**, in_recovery=false, UTF8, UTC
+  - Managed-provider identity CONFIRMED Supabase (marker roles 3/3, marker schemas 4/4)
+  - Extensions: `pg_stat_statements 1.11`, `pgcrypto 1.3`, `plpgsql 1.0`, `supabase_vault 0.3.1`, `uuid-ossp 1.1`; pinned Drizzle schema needs only core — PASS
+  - Migration state: NO drizzle journal tables (expected; `drizzle-kit push` workflow, nothing authorized yet)
+  - Catalog: `public` schema EMPTY — pinned-catalog comparison (18 tables from `lib/db/src/schema/*.ts`): present 0/18, absent 18/18, unexpected 0 → **"schema absent — pending separately authorized migration"**
+  - Rollback/redaction preserved: read-only session, transaction rolled back, zero writes
+- Full run record: `/app/memory/GATE_B_RUN_2026-08-11.md` (workspace memory; no secrets inside).
+
+**Files changed:**
+- `.agents/LOG.md` (this entry)
+- `.agents/NEXT_TASK.md` (Priority 1 status update)
+
+**Build state at end:** Application code and schema untouched. **Gate B status transition:** managed environment **VERIFIED** (connectivity, identity, version, extensions, migration state) — but the **catalog check is NOT CLEARED** (schema absent on the fresh managed database) and the runbook does not permit an empty catalog to count as PASS. Overall Gate B therefore remains **NOT CLEARED**: production event writes, activation phases, and all schema work (including the race-proof partial unique index) stay blocked until a separately authorized migration lands and the catalog check passes.
+
+**Next best action:** Operator decision on the separately authorized schema migration (`pnpm --filter @workspace/db run push` + seed policy) against the verified managed database; after it lands, re-run the read-only catalog verification (expect 18/18) and only then consider Gate B cleared. Then: race-proof partial unique index as its own reviewed schema task, and the Phase 4C stack-native port PLAN.
+
